        "original_id": "24f2ee2a-793d-598b-9bee-8fd66a1a1d52",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: George Albert Smith, Wong Jing, Stephen Chow, Cheung Man, Ng Man Tat\n- Organizations: The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints\n- Places: Salt Lake Valley\n- Products: Hail the Judge, This Is the Place Monument\n- Roles: LDS Church president, film director, producer, actor, presenter, screenwriter\n- Events: pioneers entering the Salt Lake Valley\n\nFacts:\n- George Albert Smith Sr. was born on April 4, 1870, and died on April 4, 1951.\n- George Albert Smith Sr. was an American religious leader who served as the eighth president of The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints.\n- Wong Jing was born on May 3, 1955.\n- Wong Jing is a Hong Kong film director, producer, actor, presenter, and screenwriter.\n- This Is the Place Monument was dedicated by LDS Church President George Albert Smith on July 24, 1947.\n- The dedication of This Is the Place Monument occurred on the hundredth anniversary of the pioneers entering the Salt Lake Valley.\n- Hail the Judge is a 1994 Hong Kong comedy film directed by Wong Jing.\n- Hail the Judge stars Stephen Chow, Cheung Man, and Ng Man Tat.",
